# Issues

## Critical

None found.

## Important

### I1 - Make final preservation failures fail the rehearsal and disqualify its receipt

Files: supabase/rls-tests/helpers/runR01AdoptionAtomic.ts:541-546; docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/task-9-gates.py:10.

The runner computes `modernPreserved` and `frozenInputsPreserved` in `finally`, writes them to the receipt, then exits normally even when either is false. These computations occur after the catch that sets exitCode1. Thus a successful child test plus changed frozen source or an unexpectedly changed dedicated modern database can still produce process exit0 and no receipt.error. The gate selector filters testExit/error/frozenInputsPreserved but never checks modernPreserved, so a receipt with modernPreserved:false can actually advance to all four gates. Those gates snapshot the already-changed modern state and intentionally permit their own fixture transitions; they cannot detect the earlier preservation failure.

This is a failure-path defect in a mandatory verification boundary. It does not invalidate the current receipts: the controller independently verified the supplied final flags are true. It does mean subsequent validation can report success after violating the task's readonly-source/environment contract.

Minimum fix: retain the complete receipt, but set a nonzero process exit and a clear receipt error when any required final preservation flag is not exactly true. Reject such receipts explicitly in the gate selector, including missing flags. Do not require modernBefore==modernAfter across the full-suite gates, whose authorized fixture transition is intentionally different from clone rehearsal preservation. Add an inert focused regression for false/missing final flags; preserve existing raw receipts and bind the amended executable harness to whatever final validation the controller requires.

Focused supporting check: the unchanged clone helper in the diff archive `docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/task-9-receipts/blobs/5352ca4c2660e341b88bb34519e369aa7420711bb9df7c80daff5dadd9387519.source:498-514` does enforce template preservation during close, but does not enforce the dedicated57322 state or frozen source hashes. This check prevents misattributing template enforcement to the missing runner checks.

## Minor

### M1 - Capture the deliberate error-path logging in the new HTTP tests

File: src/lib/adoptions/atomicForward.http.test.ts:37-44.

The unknown-object and nonobject cases deliberately reach the real withErrors console.error branch, so successful new tests emit an internal diagnostic and a bare42501 into the test output. The report explicitly acknowledges this noise; the archived original HTTP RED also shows it. Capture/spy on console.error for these deliberate cases, assert the expected logging if useful, and restore it in finally. This keeps genuine unexpected diagnostics visible and meets the review requirement for clean test output without changing production logging.

The reported52 lint warnings and build module-directive/bundle notices are retained baseline qualifications, not evidence of a new Task9 regression or a request to broaden this task into unrelated warning cleanup.

